    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.x\n\n### Description\n\nNot a bugreport per se, but possibly worth adding to readme, I've strugged with this issue for around an hour :)\nIf you have completeopt option to something including \"menu\" or \"menuone\", autocomplete will insert results right after typing without user confirmations\n\n### Reproduction\n\n```\nvim.opt.rtp:prepend(vim.fn.stdpath \"data\" .. \"/lazy/lazy.nvim\")\nrequire \"lazy\".setup {\n    \"neovim/nvim-lspconfig\",\n    {'echasnovski/mini.completion', opts={}}}\nrequire \"lspconfig\"[\"lua_ls\"].setup{}\nvim.cmd [[ se cot=menu ]]\n```",
    "closed_at": "2025-02-22T08:18:16Z",
