        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "'mini.completion' [automatically sets suggested 'completeopt'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/f89f4e20dc998d8f0cb8b21734877a64a9adee92/doc/mini-completion.txt#L232-L235) (which is mentioned in the README) and the value is 'menuone,noselect'. Any manual setting afterwards is assumed to be done knowing the consequences of that. Managing completion is done [by built-in popup](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/f89f4e20dc998d8f0cb8b21734877a64a9adee92/doc/mini-completion.txt#L13-L14), so defining its behavior by Neovim's options is indeed an expected approach here.\n\n------\n\nSide note: I'd suggest updating Neovim to 0.10.x (latest stable version), as there are visible improvements there for 'mini.completion'. And for Nightly 0.11.x there are even more (especially if you use 'mini.icons') :)",
